{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310622,"nonce":"OfgyeWM9Iq2woFXdIB5HSFKzK10=","title":"FIXED 6eb364bd — a generic call's type argument never reached the monomorphizer; FOUR breaks in one chain, conformance 502 -\u003e 506","message":"**FIXED 6eb364bd. Conformance 502 -\u003e 506, `uncompiled` trap stubs 66 -\u003e 50,\n14 rows moved, ZERO regressions.** Closes the 25-row lever in\n[[project_uncompiled_cluster_root_census]].\n\n**THE CHAIN HAD FOUR BREAKS, not one.** Each had to be found by instrumenting;\nreading the code located none of them.\n1. **TAST never filled `type_arguments`** — empty at ~12 sites in\n   `ast_lowering/expr/calls.rs`, filled at exactly one. Added\n   `infer_call_type_arguments`: structurally unify DECLARED param types against\n   ACTUAL argument types (`Array\u003cT\u003e` vs `Array\u003cInt\u003e` reaches T).\n2. **The site was not the one I assumed.** A bare call to an INHERITED method\n   is a `FunctionCall` over a **Field** callee, NOT a MethodCall. Wiring the\n   three MethodCall sites did nothing.\n3. **`direct.rs` vetoed it**: `has_type_params` demanded the callee's\n   `signature.type_params` be visible IN THIS MODULE, which a cross-module\n   callee never is. Call-site type args are now authoritative.\n4. **The Field-callee path drops them**: `try_method_call` -\u003e\n   `try_resolved_method_call` called `build_call_direct`, which takes no type\n   args. Threaded `converted_hir_type_args` through both.\n\n**THE DECISIVE INSTRUMENT** was at the TAST-\u003eHIR boundary\n(`tast_to_hir.rs`, the three call arms), printing callee NAME + node KIND +\n`type_arguments.len()`. One build told me `aeq` was a **FunctionCall**, which\nfalsified the MethodCall assumption I had spent three builds on. **Instrument\nthe BOUNDARY, not the construction sites.**\n\n**TWO TRAPS I HIT — both cost a build cycle each:**\n- `sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head` HID the answer: `aeq` appeared twice,\n  below entries with counts of 32/12/9/8. **grep for the name you want**, do\n  not eyeball a ranked list.\n- A probe guarded on `TypedExpressionKind::Variable` misses a `FieldAccess`\n  callee. My first fall-through probe printed nothing for `aeq` for that reason\n  alone and I wrongly concluded the site was not reached.\n- A build failure hid behind `| grep -E '^error' -A 8 | head` with\n  `rc=${PIPESTATUS[0]}` printing empty. Redirect to a file and check `$?`\n  ([[feedback_never_split_a_diff_by_hunks]] records this too).\n\n**DESIGN CONSTRAINTS, keep them:**\n- ONE type parameter only. `TypeKind::Function` records NO type-param ORDER and\n  MIR consumes `type_args` POSITIONALLY, so two variables cannot be placed.\n- An UNINFORMATIVE actual (a TypeParameter, Dynamic, Unknown, Error) is SKIPPED,\n  not counted as disagreement. `aeq([1,2,3], xs)` with `xs:Array\u003cDynamic\u003e` must\n  still pin T=Int from the first argument — this was the difference between\n  \"RESOLVED\" and \"BAIL bindings disagree\".\n- `eq\u003cT\u003e(v:T,v2:T)` already worked via the erased-slot path in\n  monomorphize.rs (T is the whole param, so the slot is `i64`);\n  `aeq\u003cT\u003e(Array\u003cT\u003e,..)` had nothing to read because `Array\u003cT\u003e` erases to\n  `Ptr(Void)`. That asymmetry is why only half the cluster was failing.\n\n**SAME-CLASS IS NOT EXEMPT.** A workflow agent found that a same-class\n`garr\u003cX\u003e(Array\u003cX\u003e,Array\u003cX\u003e)` reproduces identically through the MethodCall\nbranch — cross-module inheritance was a red herring for the mechanism. Both\nshapes are wired now and `haxe-conformance/regressions/GenericCallTypeArgs.hx`\ncovers both; the CORPUS only exercises the inherited one, so the fixture is the\nonly guard on the same-class half.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_generic_call_type_args_never_reached_backend` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}